==Battleground==
*10 [[Znache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 4.67~8 seconds<sup>140f~240f</sup>.
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Formicidaean Ariant]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Formicidaean Ariant]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**10 [[Znache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**10 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage has an annoying mix of 3 enemy types, with zombies arguably being the main threat. It is a good idea to stall a bit at the start until all the Zories finish spawning to avoid the backliners being burrowed into.

On base hit, a number of fast moving peons will spawn that will disrupt specialists from hitting the bosses, shield piercers without LD will have issues hitting the boss.

Anti-zombie Long Distance units such as [[Housewife Cat]] are a good option. General anti-Behemoth options such as [[Courier Cat]] and [[Mushroom Cat]] are also good to help burn down the bosses.

